#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:5
#: 599a60ae70ad4a7ebbb754db9a03d014
msgid "Using SITL with Webots Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:7
#: 43e7bf0466ba465480460a6426d35634
msgid "ArduPilot's python-based Webots implementation is a cross-platform simulation tool that allows running ArduPilot without risking real-life crashes. This page goes over how to set up and use Webots with ArduPilot's SITL as well as touching on how to create new vehicles and worlds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:19
#: fc95366f250545ebb2db5e368499c66c
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:20
#: f9350d72a1dd45c4b0090df60ad80740
msgid "Webots itself can be downloaded from `www.cyberbotics.com <https://www.cyberbotics.com/>`__. If there is any trouble with installation see `Webots' install guide <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/guide/installation-procedure>`__ for further guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:27
#: 1a7e3b60d6114e53933db71b08e1a03f
msgid "The Webots python implementation was built for Webots 2023a and is not backward compatible. Newer versions should also work, however."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:32
#: e1c7e57640df4dd2804a826a5f52f4ed
msgid "Running the Iris Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:33
#: 159796c40342453b975758a9bee68808
msgid "The following assumes you have already successfully set up your ArduPilot dev environment (see `Building the code <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/building-the-code.html>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:37
#: 41429c9d11174337aabc7fc8110022df
msgid "Run Webots and open ``/path/to/ardupilot/libraries/SITL/examples/Webots_Python/worlds/iris.wbt`` (``File`` > ``Open World``). If everything is working you should see the simulation time advancing and no errors in the console (red warnings are fine)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:42
#: dbb406696bfb4d098f6b18faeaefcda8
msgid "Run the SITL with the following command, replacing ``/path/to/`` with your local absolute path to ardupilot::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:48
#: ef940f2e8e2b4fb2a873adc7109e426c
msgid "When running SITL in WSL2 and Webots in Windows you will have to provide the SITL with Windows' IP by adding something like ``--sim-address=172.x.x.1`` to the command above. Your exact IP can be found by running ``ipconfig`` in cmd and looking for the IP under the WSL adapter. You may also need to add WSL's IP found with ``hostname -I`` to ``iris.wbt`` so it looks something like this::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:66
#: 5d7c557d8822445bb1411389777808aa
msgid "If all goes well you should see ``Connected to ardupilot SITL`` in the Webots console. At this point, you should be able to use MAVProxy (in the SITL terminal window) or a GCS to fly the drone around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:72
#: f586b8c93e0c470fab162a47fad981bf
msgid "Other Example Worlds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:74
#: e5b18af290d04c3a91f167ff2f2d6ab4
msgid "``iris.wbt`` implements a basic quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:75
#: f41577d110a746588bc7a334fc792c15
msgid "``iris_camera.wbt`` implements a camera on a quadcopter. See ``example_camera_receive.py`` in the scripts folder for one way to get access to the camera."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:78
#: 2b9815cc8bd44eec97e1b10f82719751
msgid "``iris_depth_camera.wbt`` implements a camera that sees depth rather than color. The example camera script can also receive these images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:80
#: ac8ff0152bcf43c3ae29408f4cdb1cb2
msgid "``pioneer3at.wbt`` implements a pioneer3at rover. For the SITL command, run it with ``Rover`` instead of ``ArduCopter`` and ``pioneer3at.parm`` instead of ``iris.parm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:83
#: 93b2b29252d545d4b7e37bec5bce800b
msgid "``crazyflie.wbt`` implements a crazyflie quadcopter. Run the SITL command with ``crazyflie.parm`` instead of ``iris.parm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:85
#: bc7ddd543e5d4a34885a16e847d676be
msgid "``crazyflie_double.wbt`` implements two crazyflie drones in a swarm. For the SITL command, run it with ``crazyflie.parm`` instead of ``iris.parm`` and additionally add ``-n 2 --auto-sysid``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:91
#: 07b2d505713447f3a308ae07a88acab9
msgid "Creating a New World"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:92
#: 94c084648f5c497c8e8df8b866e44e76
msgid "Creating a new world can be done by copying an example world (such as ``iris.wbt``) and making desired changes. Prebuilt models (called `PROTOs <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/proto>`__) can be added directly through Webots by pressing ``CTRL+SHIFT+A``, or by adding them directly into the world file (`see options in documentation <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/guide/objects>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:99
#: d6b6e1dbe1814891a45e50c5b44a2695
msgid "If you want to go a bit further, check out `Webots' tutorials <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/guide/tutorial-1-your-first-simulation-in-webots>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:103
#: 15d612a0cba34b0f99c515891816cef8
msgid "An important parameter to set in every new world is the ``basicTimeStep`` parameter in the WorldInfo object. This parameter should be set to 1 or 2, as it represents how many milliseconds the simulation should delay between physics timesteps. Setting this value any higher causes ArduPilot's main loop to run too slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:111
#: 2e4c7f88849140f1b9e900da376da4d9
msgid "Creating a New Vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:112
#: 9582bb5afdc14a5a880c3908b418b231
msgid "An ArduPilot vehicle in Webots is a `Robot <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/robot>`__ object that uses the ``ardupilot_vehicle_controller.py`` controller (found in the ``controllers`` directory). This controller is run when the simulation is started and is responsible for connecting to the SITL and passing it Webots sensor information. Note that to do this it assumes that the Robot object has an `Accelerometer <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/accelerometer>`__, `Gyro <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/gyro>`__, `InertialUnit <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/inertialunit>`__, and `GPS <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/gps>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:123
#: 8df4381ecc644ea1a632bf8a2809c5c4
msgid "To create a new vehicle that can be used in multiple worlds, like the Iris model, we can create a `PROTO <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/proto>`__ file which will describe the vehicle (a Robot object) and be importable into any world. The simplest way to do this is to copy the ``iris.proto`` file in the ``protos`` folder and edit or remove components (such as propellers, mesh, and the extension slot). If you want to start from scratch, you can look at the `documentation for creating a PROTO file <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/reference/proto-definition>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-python.rst:131
#: ae15bc143d694a1bb7eccf7ee4401271
msgid "Of particular note, the Robot object has a property called ``controllerArgs`` which are passed to the controller when the simulation is run, allowing us to specify traits of the vehicle such as motor names, count, and directions. The full list of available arguments are documented in ``ardupilot_vehicle_controller.py``."
msgstr ""
